f:["$","$L17",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#the-problem","title":"The problem"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-ships-in-local-remote-execution","title":["What ships in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"@local-remote-execution"}]]},{"depth":2,"url":"#set-it-up","title":"Set it up"},{"depth":3,"url":"#install-nix-with-flakes-enabled","title":"Install Nix with flakes enabled"},{"depth":3,"url":"#pull-the-template","title":"Pull the template"},{"depth":3,"url":"#initialise-git-before-you-enter-the-shell","title":"Initialise git before you enter the shell"},{"depth":3,"url":"#enter-the-dev-shell","title":"Enter the dev shell"},{"depth":3,"url":"#point-userbazelrc-at-your-cluster","title":["Point ",["$","code",null,{"children":"user.bazelrc"}]," at your cluster"]},{"depth":3,"url":"#build","title":"Build"},{"depth":2,"url":"#adding-lre-to-a-project-you-already-have","title":"Adding LRE to a project you already have"},{"depth":2,"url":"#troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting"},{"depth":2,"url":"#faq","title":"FAQ"}],"full":"$undefined","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"children":"Toolchains and hermeticity"}],["$","$L19",null,{"children":"Your action ran on a worker and failed on a missing compiler. Here is why that happens, and how to pin the toolchain so local and remote builds hash identically."}],["$","$L1a",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," anyone whose actions execute remotely but fail on the\nworker for reasons that never happen locally. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}],"\na Nix-pinned toolchain that produces the same action digests on your machine\nand on a worker. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," thirty minutes for the walkthrough."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"data-prerequisites":true,"className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"my-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand","children":"Before you start"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground [&>p]:my-0","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["A cache serving hits to your build. If you don't have one yet, start with ",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/getting-started","children":"Getting started"}],"."]}]}]]}],"\n",["$","$L1c",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-problem","children":"The problem"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"An action is a closed description of some work: input digests, a command\nline, an environment, and platform properties. If the compiler your command\ninvokes isn't in that description, the action is a lie: it works on your\nmachine because your machine happens to have the compiler, and it fails on a\nworker that doesn't."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["This is not a Forge behaviour. It is what remote execution ",["$","em",null,{"children":"is"}],": the\nprotocol will faithfully reproduce whatever you described, and no more.\nCaching lets you get away with an under-described action because the only\nmachine that ever ran it was yours. Execution doesn't."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Two ways out exist."}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Make the environment part of the image."}]," Bake the toolchain into the\nworker's container, and route actions to it with the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"container-image"}],"\nproperty. Minimal, and it's what most fleets do first.\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/containers-and-images","children":"Containers and images"}]," covers\nthis path."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Make the toolchain part of the action."}]," Pin every tool at a\ncontent-addressed path so the toolchain itself is an input the CAS knows\nabout. This is Local Remote Execution, and it's the rest of this page."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["The second is strictly stronger: it gets you identical action digests\nlocally and remotely, which means a local build and a remote build share\ncache entries instead of each maintaining their own.\n","$L1d"," is the conceptual write-up; this\npage is the mechanism."]}],"\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24","\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31","\n","$L32","\n","$L33"]}],"$L34"]}]
