24:["$","p",null,{"children":["The flake module always emits the Rust platform and toolchain flags, and adds\nthe C++ ones only on Linux, where the generated config is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"x86_64"}]," and\ncarries a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"container-image"}]," property. On an ",["$","code",null,{"children":"x86_64-linux"}]," host that means\nC++ actions can run locally out of the same ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/nix/store"}]," paths the worker\nimage has, or remotely on that image, with the same digest either way. On\nmacOS there is no local C++ or Java toolchain at all, so those actions can\nonly execute on a remote worker running the matching image, and even a\nNix-pinned toolchain costs a network round-trip: ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"LRE gives you\nhermeticity, not offline-ness."}]]}]
